From: Llaminar native progress regression
Subject: [PATCH] Publish ordering events from the completed native SDMA frontier

A timing-disabled hipEventRecord after a required NoCU copy currently queues
a compute barrier. Physical queues are shared after the native queue bound is
reached, so that barrier can sit behind an unrelated peer-held captured graph.
The DMA completion is already zero, but hipEventQuery remains not ready. If
the graph awaits expert movement certified by that event, this forms a cycle.

For an uncaptured ordering-only event with no pending compute/cache fence,
external dependency or raw queue wait, retain the exact native SDMA signal.
ROCr's copy completion already certifies system-coherent bytes. Preserve the
signal reference and normal coalescing lifecycle rather than generating an
unrelated compute fence. Timing, IPC, callback, captured and compute frontiers
retain their existing implementations and scopes. No queue limit, allocation
policy, host synchronization, packet batching or stream priority is changed.

Pinned base: ROCm/rocm-systems 6b0e43f341195e203754e08f850e437ff2fc09f9
             (therock-10.0, ROCm Core SDK 10.0.0)

diff --git a/rocclr/device/rocm/rocvirtual.hpp b/rocclr/device/rocm/rocvirtual.hpp
--- a/rocclr/device/rocm/rocvirtual.hpp
+++ b/rocclr/device/rocm/rocvirtual.hpp
@@ -299,6 +299,15 @@ class VirtualGPU : public device::VirtualDevice {
     //! Empty check for external signals
     bool IsExternalSignalListEmpty() const { return external_signals_.empty(); }
 
+    /**
+     * @brief Whether the exact last SDMA signal covers this logical FIFO.
+     * Pending cross-queue dependencies must still be submitted, so their
+     * existence prohibits substituting an earlier copy's completion signal.
+     */
+    bool HasOrderedSdmaCompletion() const {
+      return IsSdmaEngine(engine_) && external_signals_.empty() && dynamic_queue_waits_.empty();
+    }
+
     //! Adds a raw signal for dependency tracking
     void AddDynamicQueueWait(hsa_signal_t signal) { dynamic_queue_waits_.push_back(signal); }
 
diff --git a/rocclr/device/rocm/rocvirtual.cpp b/rocclr/device/rocm/rocvirtual.cpp
--- a/rocclr/device/rocm/rocvirtual.cpp
+++ b/rocclr/device/rocm/rocvirtual.cpp
@@ -5072,6 +5072,26 @@ void VirtualGPU::submitMarker(amd::Marker& vcmd) {
           reinterpret_cast<uintptr_t>(vcmd.ipcCompletionSignal()->getHandle()));
     }
 
+    // A required SDMA copy already publishes system-coherent completion. An
+    // ordering-only event names that exact frontier; routing its receipt
+    // through a shared compute queue can place it behind an unrelated graph
+    // waiting for this very receipt. Retain the native signal instead. The
+    // reference prevents signal-pool reuse until every event consumer retires.
+    // Real timing, IPC, capture, callbacks and outstanding compute/cache work
+    // still require their ordinary marker implementation and fence scopes.
+    if (vcmd.coalesceEvent() != 0 && !vcmd.profilingInfo().enabled_ &&
+        !vcmd.getPktCapturingState() && vcmd.Callback() == nullptr &&
+        ipc_s.handle == 0 && vcmd.ipcDepSignal() == nullptr &&
+        !hasPendingDispatch_ && !isFenceDirty() &&
+        Barriers().HasOrderedSdmaCompletion()) {
+      auto* completion = Barriers().GetLastSignal();
+      AttachHwEvent(command_, completion);
+      SetCoalesceWindow(vcmd.coalesceEvent(), completion);
+      profilingEnd();
+      force_irq_ = false;
+      return;
+    }
+
